# Divine Intervention enters with two intervention counters (CR 614.1c, 122.6); at the beginning of its controller's upkeep
# its ability removes one (CR 503.1a, 122.1), and none on the opponent's; when that removes the last one, its controller
# having removed it, the game is a draw (CR 104.4c): nobody wins and nobody loses. Cast on turn 1 off zero-cost mana for
# exactly its {6}{W}{W}; the counters are checked after each of turn 2's, 3's and 4's upkeeps, so one counter more or less
# moves the draw to another turn, and the game ends in turn 5's upkeep with neither player having lost.

[Bot1 Deck]
Divine Intervention
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

